- The Chinese word for "correct" (正确 / 正確, also 正确的 / 正確的) gives a strong
  positive value; the word for "wrong / error" (错误 / 錯誤) a weaker positive one.
- The first token of each document has no earlier context, so its value depends only on
  the token itself. Code and markup starts (#, import, package, <|im_start|>) are
  positive; a lowercase function word with a leading space (of, in, for, the, a, ...) is
  negative; other tokens are small by kind: punctuation, CJK and other non-ASCII, and
  lowercase starts positive, a lone space slightly negative, capitalised words and digits
  about zero.
- Everywhere else the value is 0.
