"""Sparse approximation: question-mark operators versus overrides and collocations.

Positive pulses mark optional/null syntax, repeated question marks, and some
formatting runs. Negative pulses mark override declarations and phrases such
as 'big picture' and 'big screen'. These are separate observed patterns, not
one unified meaning. Most text gets zero; token-specific background effects
are not modeled. Only a short, document-local text buffer is retained.
