negative class mean, with larger magnitudes for recognizable syntax/control
openers and the second digit of a leading '12'. Initial repetitions retain
that response. Further rules cover interpuncts, superscripts, formatting
punctuation, shading, I-like Greek/Cyrillic letters, LaTeX list syntax, and a
few URL/filename patterns. Split UTF-8 flags and runes are positive; split
Braille depends on the number of raised dots in its right column.

This is a partial approximation: it omits most word-specific variation.
State resets at document boundaries; text history is limited to 32 bytes.
