Standalone helping characters have the strongest negative response; merged
helping phrases are weaker. 忙 ('busy'), its helping idioms, and English 'bang'
also respond. Small secondary rules cover knowing, banking and reading links.
Document starts get a small negative baseline, with two positive exceptions:
'Title:' and '12' at their second token.
This is a spelling-based approximation, not a general detector of helpfulness.
